```java
@Test
void shouldThrowWhenDivideByZero() {
    ArithmeticException ex = assertThrows(
        ArithmeticException.class,
        () -> calculator.divide(10, 0)
    );
    assertEquals("/ by zero", ex.getMessage());
}
```
assertThrows returns the caught exception, so you can inspect its message, cause, or properties. If the code doesn't throw, the test fails. If it throws a different exception type, the test also fails.
